  "body": "Requested by the user (2026-11-11). The sibling issue adds ER collet chucks; this one adds the **taper (spindle-side) holders** they mount in.\n\n**What:** built-in taper holders as revolved profiles, each covering the taper's flange (V-flange and gripper groove) as the part that matters for clearance, plus the front body:\n- **BT30, BT40** (JIS B 6339 / MAS 403), with **CAT40** (ANSI/ASME B5.50) for the US;\n- **research step first:** confirm whether the small BT sizes in the user's \"BT10-40\" range (BT10, BT15, BT20, BT25) are standard sizes for small or high-speed spindles, and include the ones that are, with their sources;\n- **variants:** each taper in an **ER collet chuck** version (ER16 / ER25 / ER32, sharing the sibling issue's ER geometry) and a **Weldon (side-lock) end-mill holder** version (DIN 1835 form B / DIN 6359 bore sizes, e.g. 6-20 mm and 1/4-3/4 in).\n\nDimensions come from the public standards, recorded as typical values. Original profiles; no vendor model is copied. The gauge length and projection are adjustable.\n\nEffort: high.\n\n**Done means:**\n- Every listed taper and variant can be picked in the tool editor.\n- The collision checks judge it.\n- Pinned by a flange-strikes-the-fixture test, and a test that a long-reach Weldon holder clears where a short one would collide.\n\nPart of #743.\n",
